<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Interwar period</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The interwar period lasted from 11 November 1918 to 1 September 1939, from the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">World War I</a> to the beginning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">World War II</a>. The prosperous Roaring Twenties, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/automobile">automobiles</a>, electric lighting and radio became common, were followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, which severely damaged many of the largest economies. The Russian, Ottoman, Austro-Hungarian and German empires were dismantled, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was formed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> became independent. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communism">Communism</a> rose from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>, fascism rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and the territorial ambitions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, Italy and Germany led to the expansion of their domains.</p></div>
